in":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/d3b16d3edf3d4be93b60d42fa4b1509d337b86b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:12:15Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:12:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(VCST-6210): cherry-pick vc-frontend#2550 — workflow opt-in variables (#5)\n\n## Description\n\nBrings **only** VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend#2550 into Next, as a\ncherry-pick (`git cherry-pick -x 596bad0ac`). The 8 vc-frontend PRs\nmerged before it (incl. the Module Federation ones,\nVirtoCommerce/vc-frontend#2480 and VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend#2481) stay\nfor the next full upstream merge.\n\nWhat it does here: with the repository variables already set in this\nrepo (`VC_CI=true`, `VC_RELEASE=true`,\n`SONAR_PROJECT_KEY=VirtoCommerce_vc-frontend-next`), CI, CodeQL,\nSecurity, pin-check, workflow-guards and the release workflows run in\nNext once Actions are enabled; Sonar reports to\n`VirtoCommerce_vc-frontend-next`; the Storybook image is\n`vc-frontend-next-storybook` and the zips\n`vc-frontend-next-<version>.zip` (from the package name, #4). Cloud\ndeploys, Jira steps and auto-tests stay off.\n\n### The one conflict\n\n`theme-ci.yml`, SonarCloud Scan: Dependabot (#1) had bumped\n`sonarqube-scan-action` to v8.3.0 here, while vc-frontend#2550 added\n`with: args` under v8.2.0. Resolved as v8.3.0 + `args` (v8.3.0 still has\n`args`, default `\"\"`).\n\n### Checked\n\n- The change set is line-for-line the one in vc-frontend#2550 (sorted\n`+`/`-` lines of both diffs compared: identical).\n- Every job''s guard still passes the `workflow-guards.yml` rule (run\nlocally).\n\n### Next upstream merge\n\nIt will meet these same changes again from `upstream/dev`; identical\nhunks merge without conflict. If the SonarCloud step conflicts, keep\nNext''s action version and the `args` line.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6210","tree":{"sha":"01b1cc5af70399cbfa9a3b921fd3f940e32fc3b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/trees/01b1cc5af70399cbfa9a3b921fd3f940e32fc3b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/commits/d3b16d3edf3d4be93b60d42fa4b1509d337b86b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 01b1cc5af70399cbfa9a3b921fd3f940e32fc3b4\nparent af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1\nparent ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1791465135 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791465135 +0100\n\nci(VCST-6210): cherry-pick vc-frontend#2550 — workflow opt-in variables (#5)\n\n## Description\n\nBrings **only** VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend#2550 into Next, as a\ncherry-pick (`git cherry-pick -x 596bad0ac`). The 8 vc-frontend PRs\nmerged before it (incl. the Module Federation ones,\nVirtoCommerce/vc-frontend#2480 and VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend#2481) stay\nfor the next full upstream merge.\n\nWhat it does here: with the repository variables already set in this\nrepo (`VC_CI=true`, `VC_RELEASE=true`,\n`SONAR_PROJECT_KEY=VirtoCommerce_vc-frontend-next`), CI, CodeQL,\nSecurity, pin-check, workflow-guards and the release workflows run in\nNext once Actions are enabled; Sonar reports to\n`VirtoCommerce_vc-frontend-next`; the Storybook image is\n`vc-frontend-next-storybook` and the zips\n`vc-frontend-next-<version>.zip` (from the package name, #4). Cloud\ndeploys, Jira steps and auto-tests stay off.\n\n### The one conflict\n\n`theme-ci.yml`, SonarCloud Scan: Dependabot (#1) had bumped\n`sonarqube-scan-action` to v8.3.0 here, while vc-frontend#2550 added\n`with: args` under v8.2.0. Resolved as v8.3.0 + `args` (v8.3.0 still has\n`args`, default `\"\"`).\n\n### Checked\n\n- The change set is line-for-line the one in vc-frontend#2550 (sorted\n`+`/`-` lines of both diffs compared: identical).\n- Every job''s guard still passes the `workflow-guards.yml` rule (run\nlocally).\n\n### Next upstream merge\n\nIt will meet these same changes again from `upstream/dev`; identical\nhunks merge without conflict. If the SonarCloud step conflicts, keep\nNext''s action version and the `args` line.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6210","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5avCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUawQAGE2X6dg7g2AYO8JPUXd7y8A\n5EHFeuzcpCEefJBLhbUgGjrLJgVj4pIJvZBHd3TAtAdMpEhexCfLJyMzGsKrxzd/\nTBW4BKHbHKh48d/C8Q6kaGjLAVRqOQAdxLddju1t3SgmkYYjU3jGkIF7GD2ebD83\njglIYFPjxwZObYFMW0USoj46PsywqLfanQei6upCMqc7RM5/EuPEyYkZ3nPlNe/1\nlbuswCQ2ycqH121qXVw6DDuXpy9d4AMTnwJsdqloTSPK2wOZKVkvSmGVOGBjnvHc\n6wc9pbQEtiaJdkugRXskhOpIKvOzgTirjwghmR4KZO/G+YUuiMKE98lr5PZSO87m\nyAp79fL5NCTl5MYgdADaL5qfeJwTECsQ951QghZdPPVYA9w1kUquK2CgfSPDvQI3\nuP70eeyFQA2+wM7/d266zD4e2MgJCJFWlJFZf3gYCaESbbUQlQgOCe5GMF2ShwNk\nGfUf9rEOKs32I77Bf1Qk18qqC64nue6GjHoz4ncpwqmOAPT0P/F+Q0WQKZx2Av0J\n4QU97nLhE57yI+lhUCF21M36DJIthezbfS6pMi2C4BYi9YdJb1s0u3KNY8dYrlPa\ncr/iikRMtLO9eDzAmdsO57L+RDfoD46x8SyJCzp6pEqTDnKHOmwRSicOESyxMcxS\nFzWfD2Df4QQsmGIgxA2D\n=i0Rs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T13:12:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/d3b16d3edf3d4be93b60d42fa4b1509d337b86b2","node_id":"C_kwDOU_T1lNoAKGQzYjE2ZDNlZGYzZDRiZTkzYjYwZDQyZmE0YjE1MDlkMzM3Yjg2YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1","sha":"af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e","sha":"ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e"}],"sha":"d3b16d3edf3d4be93b60d42fa4b1509d337b86b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/d3b16d3edf3d4be93b60d42fa4b1509d337b86b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:06:21Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:08:07Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"message":"ci(VCST-6210): let another repository opt in to the workflows with repository variables (#2550)\n\nvc-frontend-next carries these workflows too, but every job is guarded\nby vc-frontend''s repo id (#2530), so nothing runs there. This PR lets\nanother repository **opt in** to each group of jobs with a repository\nvariable, and write to its **own** Sonar project, Storybook image and\narchives, never to vc-frontend''s.\n\n**vc-frontend does not change.** The repo id stays the first alternative\nof every guard, and every new variable falls back to today''s value.\nNothing needs to be set here before or after merging. The private theme\nmirror and forks set neither the id nor the variables, so nothing runs\nthere, as before.\n\nWas `github.repository_id == ''296335982''`, now `(github.repository_id ==\n''296335982'' || vars.VC_<KIND> == ''true'')`:\n\n| Variable | Jobs / steps |\n|---|---|\n| `VC_CI` | theme-ci `ci`, storybook-ci `ci`, CodeQL, Security\n(`semgrep`, `osv-scanner`), pin-check, workflow-guards |\n| `VC_E2E` | theme-ci `auto-tests` |\n| `VC_RELEASE` | release, core-facade-release, theme-release-hotfix |\n\n**The cloud deploys and the Jira steps stay vc-frontend-only.** The\ndeploys (`deploy-cloud` in theme-ci, storybook-ci and\n`deploy-cloud.yml`) target vc-frontend''s environments. The Jira steps\n(\"Push Build Info to Jira\" in theme-ci and storybook-ci, \"Update Jira\nTasks with Release Number\" in theme-ci) would put another repository''s\nbuilds and release numbers on the same tickets; since their job may now\nrun elsewhere, they check `github.repository_id == ''296335982''`\nthemselves.\n\n| Variable | Where | Unset (vc-frontend) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SONAR_PROJECT_KEY` | `-Dsonar.projectKey` in the theme-ci and\ntheme-release-hotfix scans | `sonar-project.properties` |\n| `E2E_TEST_SUITES` | theme-ci `auto-tests` `testSuites` |\n`graphql,e2e,restapi` |\n\nThe `E2E_TEST_SUITES` fallback has to stay in the caller: a `with:`\ninput cannot be left out conditionally, and an empty `testSuites` runs\nno suite at all in `run-pytest-tests` (each suite is gated by\n`contains(inputs.testSuites, …)`), so the job would pass green with no\ntests.\n\n**Named after the package:** the build zips already were (`$(jq -r .name\npackage.json)-<version>.zip` in the shared org Blob container); the\nStorybook image now is too, `<name>-storybook`, instead of a hard-coded\n`vc-theme-b2b-vue-storybook`. Here that gives the same name as before;\nvc-frontend-next renames its package, so its zips and image are its own.\nA name that is not a valid image name (e.g. a scoped `@x/y`) fails the\nstep.\n\n- The checker accepts the new form for `VC_CI`, `VC_E2E` and\n`VC_RELEASE`, and still rejects every other form.\n- `.github/workflows/README.md` gets a section, \"Running the workflows\nin another repository\".\n- Each job''s existing guard comment now names its variable too.\n\n- **CI on this PR (vc-frontend):** `guards`, `pinact`, CodeQL, Semgrep,\nOSV-Scanner, Sonar and theme-ci `ci` pass, `deploy-cloud` is skipped as\non any PR. `auto-tests` ran all three suites (graphql, e2e, restapi)\nwith the `E2E_TEST_SUITES` fallback; one matrix leg (postgres,\nopensearch) failed on a single e2e test,\n`test_checkout_payment_method_single_page`, which passed in the other\nlegs.\n- **The checker logic passes on all workflows** (its guard regex and\n`&&` rule, run locally over every job with a Python stand-in for `yq`),\nand every job''s guard was classified: 11 opt-in, 3 id-only (the cloud\ndeploys), 2 mirror-only.\n- **Not run by this PR''s CI: the Storybook image name.** storybook-ci\nruns only on push to `master`/`dev` and on dispatch, and a dispatch from\nthis branch would push the `latest` tag. The step was checked locally:\n`vc-theme-b2b-vue` gives `vc-theme-b2b-vue-storybook` (the name used\ntoday), `vc-frontend-next` gives `vc-frontend-next-storybook`, `@x/y`\nand `Foo` fail the step. The first real run is the push to `dev` after\nmerging.\n\nVCST-6210''s settings for vc-frontend-next are agreed. Merging it early\nis harmless, since vc-frontend behaves the same; Next only starts\nrunning jobs once its variables are set and Actions are enabled there.\n\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6210\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.60.0-pr-2550-7127-7127ba0a.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Kubyshkin <andrew.kubyshkin@virtoway.com>\n(cherry picked from commit 596bad0ac504e61a80a375101f334ff0dd92c358)","tree":{"sha":"01b1cc5af70399cbfa9a3b921fd3f940e32fc3b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/trees/01b1cc5af70399cbfa9a3b921fd3f940e32fc3b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/commits/ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e","node_id":"C_kwDOU_T1lNoAKGZmMDc2NDk4YjY0MDYzYWY0NzMxYmI0OWYyNzU2Nzk5MTI1NGYzMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1","sha":"af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1"}],"sha":"ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/ff076498b64063af4731bb49f27567991254f32e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:26:48Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:26:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(VCST-6210): name the package vc-frontend-next (#4)\n\n## Description\n\nRenames the root package from `vc-theme-b2b-vue` to\n**`vc-frontend-next`**.\n\n**Why:** CI names its build archives after this field\n(`<name>-<version>.zip`, in theme-ci and storybook-ci) and publishes\nthem to the organization''s **shared** Blob container\n`vc3prerelease/packages`, next to vc-frontend''s and every backend\nmodule''s (`VirtoCommerce.Catalog_…`, `VirtoCommerce.Cart_…`, …). Under\nupstream''s name, a Next build would overwrite a vc-frontend build as\nsoon as the versions matched. With its own name, Next can use the shared\ncontainer and the org `BLOB_URL`/`BLOB_TOKEN` like every other\nrepository, with no container or token of its own.\n\n- Archives become `vc-frontend-next-<version>.zip`. The hotfix workflow\nalready names its archive after the repository, so all of Next''s\narchives now share one prefix.\n- Nothing else reads the name: the shared actions (`get-image-version`,\n`publish-blob-release`) take only the version from `package.json`.\n- `yarn.lock`: the two `@workspace:.` lines follow the new name (`yarn\ninstall`).\n- vc-frontend has not changed this field since 2022, so later merges\nfrom it are unlikely to touch this line.\n\n### Verification\n- `yarn install`: only the two lock lines change.\n- `yarn build-only`: passes.\n- `jq -r .name package.json` → `vc-frontend-next`, so the archive is\n`vc-frontend-next-3.0.0.zip`.\n\n> ⚠️ This repo is a fork of vc-frontend. Merge with **\"Create a merge\ncommit\"**, not squash. A squash is harmless for this PR itself, but keep\nthe habit for upstream merges.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6210\n### Artifact URL:","tree":{"sha":"e96f637bd50e147fd53eed9dbd9bdc80ae5f9d23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/trees/e96f637bd50e147fd53eed9dbd9bdc80ae5f9d23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/commits/af26d911f5695c0f8cf938b306fedb33c887e9d1","verification":{"payload":"tree e96f637bd50e147fd53eed9dbd9bdc80ae5f9d23\nparent 93e2980a1c446b2ac9f047b644a69214b0611224\nparent 1556e8fad435aa763ddebc1677b601840aca3256\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1791455208 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791455208 +0100\n\nchore(VCST-6210): name the package vc-frontend-next (#4)\n\n## Description\n\nRenames the root package from `vc-theme-b2b-vue` to\n**`vc-frontend-next`**.\n\n**Why:** CI names its build archives after this field\n(`<name>-<version>.zip`, in theme-ci and storybook-ci) and publishes\nthem to the organization''s **shared** Blob container\n`vc3prerelease/packages`, next to vc-frontend''s and every backend\nmodule''s (`VirtoCommerce.Catalog_…`, `VirtoCommerce.Cart_…`, …). Under\nupstream''s name, a Next build would overwrite a vc-frontend build as\nsoon as the versions matched. With its own name, Next can use the shared\ncontainer and the org `BLOB_URL`/`BLOB_TOKEN` like every other\nrepository, with no container or token of its own.\n\n- Archives become `vc-frontend-next-<version>.zip`. The hotfix workflow\nalready names its archive after the repository, so all of Next''s\narchives now share one prefix.\n- Nothing else reads the name: the shared actions (`get-image-version`,\n`publish-blob-release`) take only the version from `package.json`.\n- `yarn.lock`: the two `@workspace:.` lines follow the new name (`yarn\ninstall`).\n- vc-frontend has not changed this field since 2022, so later merges\nfrom it are unlikely to touch this line.\n\n### Verification\n- `yarn install`: only the two lock lines change.\n- `yarn build-only`: passes.\n- `jq -r .name package.json` → `vc-frontend-next`, so the archive is\n`vc-frontend-next-3.0.0.zip`.\n\n> ⚠️ This repo is a fork of vc-frontend. Merge with **\"Create a merge\ncommit\"**, not squash. A squash is harmless for this PR itself, but keep\nthe habit for upstream merges.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6210\n### Artifact URL:","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx2/oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5U8QAK+gTKdtofTGCIahRYnnIXs0\np8m6VHlkFNiEwXVkIzl7+eIuKT59N6V4XqxvXg7PhuqNMnEUZBofRjEpmimTDtmI\nGKP0WGTBEpoI+tSdtw3xljOPpx3Rf2dGiR8/OS/xrIXGsgAJkikw6TUX/zjOMQEx\nsX2rj2bjol4hlxFpYBrurllDyZOJj0PW5Z+A7LiphzLutkYR5TP6i/OKkvvGkV9Z\nUf3lgvQdQdAhGNGC08u0wRcCKoZtjag4j5LH5bgROIGZjiHKnL1nUowMprDsys5T\n47k/OulEB7g4lXQwGCkZjtchomn0+hbHEpG3snT9MOWSNbzGdd+FOMCSfBjOQszk\n8FJSGoDc3Ir8R8gQrFbms8vMHfz7TcCgCiKOXMgjNZg7kQONb3UO3OuYrgYgrOVA\nTouvzPBuTCrS4W+Kl8d6A/HxdvGtBJ6Iw6FYX1PZ7HMYI74h/RPLeUlJyZyC3Ows\nLgnKr4Q9W74J7eVhfIbz/jtKUljlk1BiBSO12QU5thbZ5CVx2er+ruW+pIXkT0p8\n6/ZU0anSVrAd3i+hfTMFU+/mC+JqWda2FYJ6nUtabdRiIyG356tIAJp9+hHvH2dR\nbkWpLOvST6YyHHoS8+5rQ5tuJohWp6axtiPeHkGB3DQrakikf0bG