.com/users/vas11yev1work/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vas11yev1work","id":49168917,"login":"vas11yev1work","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTY4OTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/4fe2994927d4b9d3c3557ef7857e76a75b9b2aa9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:35:57Z","email":"49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anatolii Vasilev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:35:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5957): missions redesign (#2524)\n\nBrings the Missions & challenges page in line with the updated design.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Banners**\n- `light` / `dark` variants replaced with `primary` / `info` colors:\nwhite surface, 4px accent on the start edge, solid icon circle with a\nwhite Lucide glyph, shadow.\n- Uppercase 14px title; \"Virto Rewards balance\" moved from\n`PointsBalance` into the banner title.\n- \"Points history\" is now a `VcButton sm soft` instead of a text link.\n\n**Mission card**\n- Banner is 210px tall, gradient overlay removed.\n- Points and mission type are shown as tonal chips (warning / info) with\nsolid icons, side by side at the top. The uppercase type caption is\nremoved.\n- Completed missions get a `success-400` @ 75% overlay with a 56px\n`circle-check`, replacing the \"Completed\" chip.\n- Body order: progress label → bar → title; the footer holds the\ndeadline badge and a `sm outline` action button.\n- `md` shadow; grid gap 16 → 20px.\n\n**Progress and deadline**\n- Progress bar is `info-500`, and `success-500` once the mission is\ncompleted (card and order modal).\n- Deadline dot follows the design thresholds: ≤15 days → danger, 16–30 →\nwarning, >30 or no deadline → success. Completed missions stay success.\nThe dot uses the `-500` fill.\n\n**SKU mission modal**\n- Width increased to 60rem.\n- Products render in `VcLineItems` with Product / Properties (SKU) /\nPrice per item / Quantity / Total columns.\n- Missing availability flags now default to `false`. Before,\n`QuantityControl` read a missing flag as `true`, so an out-of-stock\nproduct could still be added.\n\n**Cleanup**\n- Removed the unused `card.completed` locale key.\n\nSorting controls from the design are out of scope.\n\n## Testing\n- `vitest run client-app/modules/loyalty` passes; threshold tests\nupdated.\n- Lint and type-check pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2524-3069-30691594.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f72534624c1ca5506171aacd080c84427bf47f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/trees/4f72534624c1ca5506171aacd080c84427bf47f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/commits/4fe2994927d4b9d3c3557ef7857e76a75b9b2aa9","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f72534624c1ca5506171aacd080c84427bf47f3\nparent 15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72\nauthor Anatolii Vasilev <49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com> 1790926557 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790926557 +0200\n\nfeat(VCST-5957): missions redesign (#2524)\n\nBrings the Missions & challenges page in line with the updated design.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Banners**\n- `light` / `dark` variants replaced with `primary` / `info` colors:\nwhite surface, 4px accent on the start edge, solid icon circle with a\nwhite Lucide glyph, shadow.\n- Uppercase 14px title; \"Virto Rewards balance\" moved from\n`PointsBalance` into the banner title.\n- \"Points history\" is now a `VcButton sm soft` instead of a text link.\n\n**Mission card**\n- Banner is 210px tall, gradient overlay removed.\n- Points and mission type are shown as tonal chips (warning / info) with\nsolid icons, side by side at the top. The uppercase type caption is\nremoved.\n- Completed missions get a `success-400` @ 75% overlay with a 56px\n`circle-check`, replacing the \"Completed\" chip.\n- Body order: progress label → bar → title; the footer holds the\ndeadline badge and a `sm outline` action button.\n- `md` shadow; grid gap 16 → 20px.\n\n**Progress and deadline**\n- Progress bar is `info-500`, and `success-500` once the mission is\ncompleted (card and order modal).\n- Deadline dot follows the design thresholds: ≤15 days → danger, 16–30 →\nwarning, >30 or no deadline → success. Completed missions stay success.\nThe dot uses the `-500` fill.\n\n**SKU mission modal**\n- Width increased to 60rem.\n- Products render in `VcLineItems` with Product / Properties (SKU) /\nPrice per item / Quantity / Total columns.\n- Missing availability flags now default to `false`. Before,\n`QuantityControl` read a missing flag as `true`, so an out-of-stock\nproduct could still be added.\n\n**Cleanup**\n- Removed the unused `card.completed` locale key.\n\nSorting controls from the design are out of scope.\n\n## Testing\n- `vitest run client-app/modules/loyalty` passes; threshold tests\nupdated.\n- Lint and type-check pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2524-3069-30691594.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv17dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqnAQAF5Ut6oXImwBqqyxfmScfPkM\nd/D4Yeh3G08WbO81LbfhmD9cfTqKs7HX0Wuli0fKOWNB7/TITUWKx8Dx38Qrp9KB\nHomZcBfiMiQqzcDO3jVASLrIR2Js85Uxvhdma9/yq6hIThtljUxcb6iEu3JjpfgO\nP18PQOSZDzx/RuRwnnv1ZbcRXr4NcFpfX/jn8wI35kSLosM66A1mUS3tVtKDcPyF\n8b7naNTJUF61To2Elr1W0Fbe+QnncQStuXigvw2BbBSTUHJRQthU1O1XXtFQ1+hG\nzGqcRfiHPxFesfwjVFleqg0et7pO7aTp0VTkxZmBO3+A0ecNi+xVM/dc0uNtT5zM\nq3MvtjCNirj4FNumciMWgEGYbwY/UxCdtbM9o8j49u3uYV+/mPzHnEl2NU1YgGG1\ngLrOY5iw8XAIPlRshSmdO2YAbfAmXj+4pcQVwM1duRp2uUAXiOzNnK25mvzByUhv\n+odmJtg83EV2ZDgNpRMNh+vBFRvJRNSDZO6vt0ux3hXcALlzuED9Pa7r2DueheFK\niTS/N9l+jSRGZxg5MElaHO6U0j8KlOBfzHRmVz9eMK945Lhm2nkcXlRS7WGmTPvy\nmgPXrg0rIANLX8MS8VeEh5K2OmgeFQW/Ka6QfDdrk0l2KjgMuLusjLWxY2EuNgEx\no3CqGrUdOeOZcAr+FlLw\n=251V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:39:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/4fe2994927d4b9d3c3557ef7857e76a75b9b2aa9","node_id":"C_kwDOU_T1lNoAKDRmZTI5OTQ5MjdkNGI5ZDNjMzU1N2VmNzg1N2U3NmE3NWI5YjJhYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72","sha":"15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72"}],"sha":"4fe2994927d4b9d3c3557ef7857e76a75b9b2aa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/4fe2994927d4b9d3c3557ef7857e76a75b9b2aa9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46611511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muller39","id":46611511,"login":"muller39","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjExNTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:59:17Z","email":"46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Kurilin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:59:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-6077): adjust Sales Rep Hub tasks design (#2514)\n\n## Description\n\nDesign pass on the Sales Rep Hub tasks feature (VCST-5732) per the\n\"Front screens v4\" mockup, plus renaming the Calendar page to Tasks.\n\n### Tasks page (was Calendar)\n- **Task list** is a `VcTable` (zebra rows come from the table itself).\nThe checkbox column and the coloured status bars are gone.\n- **Row action**: a new Actions column with one ghost button per row:\n**Mark as complete** (`circle-check-big`, success) or **Reopen**\n(`rotate-ccw`, info). Canceled tasks get no action (previously a\ndisabled checkbox). New `sales-rep-task-action.vue`, shared by the\ndesktop cell and the mobile card. The accessible name leads with the\nvisible label (WCAG 2.5.3).\n- **Completed tasks**: the title is struck through. Titles keep the link\ncolour and still open the Edit task popup.\n- **Status chips** follow the Orders recipe (colour + variant + leading\nglyph). `tonal` is used in place of the deprecated `outline-dark`.\n- **Header**: only *New task* is left; the *Today* and *Add task*\nbuttons are removed (`goToToday` is gone from `useMonthAnchor`).\n- **Scope chips**: the chips row opens with `[date ×] Today N · All N`,\nahead of the status tabs.\n- **Today** does what the old header button did: today''s tasks\n(completed included), clears the status tab and moves the grid back to\nthe current month.\n- **Date chip**: picking a day other than today in the calendar opens a\nchip labelled with that date, with no badge. Picking another day moves\nit. Clicking it returns to that day and its month. It is closed only by\nits × (a 24px target); if its day was on screen, the page falls back to\nToday, otherwise the tab or All and the grid''s month stay as they are.\nFocus moves to Today once the chip is gone.\n- **All**: every task, with no day window and no rule; the calendar\nshows no selection.\n- `SalesRepRuleChips` gets a `#baseline` slot for this (`allLabel` is\nnow optional). New `sales-rep-task-scope-chips.vue`.\n- New `sales-rep-rule-chip.vue` (`VcTabSwitch` + label + optional count)\nis the one chip both rows render, so neither styles the other''s classes.\nThe selected chip''s count accent now follows the chip''s own selection\ninstead of the kit''s `.vc-tab-switch--checked` class; the\n`--vc-tab-switch-hover-color` override moves onto the chip. Test\nselectors `.sales-rep-rule-chips__tab / __label / __count` become\n`.sales-rep-rule-chip / __label / __count`.\n- **Counts query**: the `day` alias is replaced by `currentDay` (today''s\nwindow, resolved once) and `all`. `useSalesRepTaskCounts()` no longer\ntakes a day window.\n- **Layout**: the *Due dates* rail is 17.5rem wide with a `sm` calendar\nand sits level with the list column; the chips span the full width above\nboth. Its title is rendered inside the widget body, not as a widget\nheader, and names the `<aside>` via `aria-labelledby`.\n\n### Rename Calendar → Tasks\n- Route `/company/calendar` → `/company/tasks`, route name\n`SalesRepCalendar` → `SalesRepTasks`, plus the constants, nav link id\n(`sales-rep-tasks`) and page file (`pages/sales-rep-tasks-page.vue`, BEM\nblock `.sales-rep-tasks-page`).\n- The nav label, page H1 and breadcrumb share `tasks.title`, which now\nreads \"Tasks\". The dashboard link goes from \"Full calendar\" to \"All\ntasks\" (`tasks.view_all`, like the orders widget).\n- No redirect from the old path: VCST-5732 has not shipped in any\nrelease yet.\n\n### Dashboard tasks widget\n- The `md` calendar drops its own frame, so there is no widget inside a\nwidget. This lives in `SalesRepTaskCalendar`, so both surfaces share it.\n- Status accent bars removed from the rows.\n- The `layout-surface` rail is narrowed from 24rem to **22rem**\n(mirrored in `layout-skeleton`). This also applies to the customer\nprofile page''s rail.\n\n### ui-kit\n- `VcCalendar`: two public tokens, `--vc-calendar-border-width` (default\n`1px`) and `--vc-calendar-padding` (overrides every size; each size\nkeeps its own default padding). `SalesRepTaskCalendar` sets both to `0`\ninstead of styling `.vc-calendar` from module code.\n- `VcCalendar`: `justify-content: center` on `__weekrow`. At `sm`, a\nlong month name (\"September 2026\") makes the header wider than the seven\nfixed columns, and the day grid packed to the start with the slack on\none side.\n\n### Locales (all 13)\n- Removed: `tasks.add_task`, `tasks.full_calendar`,\n`tasks.table.complete_aria`, `tasks.table.reopen_aria`. Forks that\noverride them can drop them.\n- Added: `tasks.view_all`, `tasks.due_dates`, `tasks.all`,\n`tasks.clear_day_aria`, `tasks.table.actions`,\n`tasks.table.mark_complete`, `tasks.table.reopen`,\n`tasks.table.action_aria`.\n- Changed: `tasks.title` (\"Calendar\" → \"Tasks\").\n\n## Review notes\n- `api/graphql/types.ts` is edited by hand for `SalesRepTaskCounts`:\n`yarn generate:graphql-types` fails against the QA backend (its schema\nlacks `requestPasswordReset`). The document was rebuilt with graphql''s\n`parse` in the same shape codegen emits (checked byte-for-byte against\nthe previous committed document).\n- `sales-rep-task-action` lines its glyph up with the column heading via\n`margin-inline-start: calc((var(--px) + 2px) * -1)`, which reads\nVcButton''s size padding and its `border-2`. Left as `TODO(VCST-6133)`\nuntil the kit exposes public tokens for both.\n- Link-coloured task titles fall below 4.5:1 on a hovered row in the red\nand coffee dark presets. The cause is `VcTable`''s hard-coded hover fill,\nnot this list; follow-up in VCST-6134.\n- Month headings in longer locales (es/pt/ru) may still ellipsize in the\n17.5rem rail.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6077\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2514-96b4-96b4ee23.zip\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"95635a9a9773f0f4ff48b88b3c3d40e1eba93078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/trees/95635a9a9773f0f4ff48b88b3c3d40e1eba93078"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/commits/15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72","verification":{"payload":"tree 95635a9a9773f0f4ff48b88b3c3d40e1eba93078\nparent e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0\nauthor Alexander Kurilin <46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com> 1790924357 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790924357 +0200\n\nfeat(VCST-6077): adjust Sales Rep Hub tasks design (#2514)\n\n## Description\n\nDesign pass on the Sales Rep Hub tasks feature (VCST-5732) per the\n\"Front screens v4\" mockup, plus renaming the Calendar page to Tasks.\n\n### Tasks page (was Calendar)\n- **Task list** is a `VcTable` (zebra rows come from the table itself).\nThe checkbox column and the coloured status bars are gone.\n- **Row action**: a new Actions column with one ghost button per row:\n**Mark as complete** (`circle-check-big`, success) or **Reopen**\n(`rotate-ccw`, info). Canceled tasks get no action (previously a\ndisabled checkbox). New `sales-rep-task-action.vue`, shared by the\ndesktop cell and the mobile card. The accessible name leads with the\nvisible label (WCAG 2.5.3).\n- **Completed tasks**: the title is struck through. Titles keep the link\ncolour and still open the Edit task popup.\n- **Status chips** follow the Orders recipe (colour + variant + leading\nglyph). `tonal` is used in place of the deprecated `outline-dark`.\n- **Header**: only *New task* is left; the *Today* and *Add task*\nbuttons are removed (`goToToday` is gone from `useMonthAnchor`).\n- **Scope chips**: the chips row opens with `[date ×] Today N · All N`,\nahead of the status tabs.\n- **Today** does what the old header button did: today''s tasks\n(completed included), clears the status tab and moves the grid back to\nthe current month.\n- **Date chip**: picking a day other than today in the calendar opens a\nchip labelled with that date, with no badge. Picking another day moves\nit. Clicking it returns to that day and its month. It is closed only by\nits × (a 24px target); if its day was on screen, the page falls back to\nToday, otherwise the tab or All and the grid''s month stay as they are.\nFocus moves to Today once the chip is gone.\n- **All**: every task, with no day window and no rule; the calendar\nshows no selection.\n- `SalesRepRuleChips` gets a `#baseline` slot for this (`allLabel` is\nnow optional). New `sales-rep-task-scope-chips.vue`.\n- New `sales-rep-rule-chip.vue` (`VcTabSwitch` + label + optional count)\nis the one chip both rows render, so neither styles the other''s classes.\nThe selected chip''s count accent now follows the chip''s own selection\ninstead of the kit''s `.vc-tab-switch--checked` class; the\n`--vc-tab-switch-hover-color` override moves onto the chip. Test\nselectors `.sales-rep-rule-chips__tab / __label / __count` become\n`.sales-rep-rule-chip / __label / __count`.\n- **Counts query**: the `day` alias is replaced by `currentDay` (today''s\nwindow, resolved once) and `all`. `useSalesRepTaskCounts()` no longer\ntakes a day window.\n- **Layout**: the *Due dates* rail is 17.5rem wide with a `sm` calendar\nand sits level with the list column; the chips span the full width above\nboth. Its title is rendered inside the widget body, not as a widget\nheader, and names the `<aside>` via `aria-labelledby`.\n\n### Rename Calendar → Tasks\n- Route `/company/calendar` → `/company/tasks`, route name\n`SalesRepCalendar` → `SalesRepTasks`, plus the constants, nav link id\n(`sales-rep-tasks`) and page file (`pages/sales-rep-tasks-page.vue`, BEM\nblock `.sales-rep-tasks-page`).\n- The nav label, page H1 and breadcrumb share `tasks.title`, which now\nreads \"Tasks\". The dashboard link goes from \"Full calendar\" to \"All\ntasks\" (`tasks.view_all`, like the orders widget).\n- No redirect from the old path: VCST-5732 has not shipped in any\nrelease yet.\n\n### Dashboard tasks widget\n- The `md` calendar drops its own frame, so there is no widget inside a\nwidget. This lives in `SalesRepTaskCalendar`, so both surfaces share it.\n- Status accent bars removed from the rows.\n- The `layout-surface` rail is narrowed from 24rem to **22rem**\n(mirrored in `layout-skeleton`). This also applies to the customer\nprofile page''s rail.\n\n### ui-kit\n- `VcCalendar`: two public tokens, `--vc-calendar-border-width` (default\n`1px`) and `--vc-calendar-padding` (overrides every size; each size\nkeeps its own default padding). `SalesRepTaskCalendar` sets both to `0`\ninstead of styling `.vc-calendar` from module code.\n- `VcCalendar`: `justify-content: center` on `__weekrow`. At `sm`, a\nlong month name (\"September 2026\") makes the header wider than the seven\nfixed columns, and the day grid packed to the start with the slack on\none side.\n\n### Locales (all 13)\n- Removed: `tasks.add_task`, `tasks.full_calendar`,\n`tasks.table.complete_aria`, `tasks.table.reopen_aria`. Forks that\noverride them can drop them.\n- Added: `tasks.view_all`, `tasks.due_dates`, `tasks.all`,\n`tasks.clear_day_aria`, `tasks.table.actions`,\n`tasks.table.mark_complete`, `tasks.table.reopen`,\n`tasks.table.action_aria`.\n- Changed: `tasks.title` (\"Calendar\" → \"Tasks\").\n\n## Review notes\n- `api/graphql/types.ts` is edited by hand for `SalesRepTaskCounts`:\n`yarn generate:graphql-types` fails against the QA backend (its schema\nlacks `requestPasswordReset`). The document was rebuilt with graphql''s\n`parse` in the same shape codegen emits (checked byte-for-byte against\nthe previous committed document).\n- `sales-rep-task-action` lines its glyph up with the column heading via\n`margin-inline-start: calc((var(--px) + 2px) * -1)`, which reads\nVcButton''s size padding and its `border-2`. Left as `TODO(VCST-6133)`\nuntil the kit exposes public tokens for both.\n- Link-coloured task titles fall below 4.5:1 on a hovered row in the red\nand coffee dark presets. The cause is `VcTable`''s hard-coded hover fill,\nnot this list; follow-up in VCST-6134.\n- Month headings in longer locales (es/pt/ru) may still ellipsize in the\n17.5rem rail.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6077\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2514-96b4-96b4ee23.zip\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv1ZFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/MoQACAnfmR2VZ+HivGfQSZIXo37\ngJsKcEkwjhY2dz+B7WzlsXRqdhgHvlMcMjZQLhim0fxeXjZouCeZHN583Uvz4fhB\niGsLz/1N0U14gOUBnnne2pApDAHhJp/g5DS6TqYcbd4Kl1P+3qnQh/V2Xdj5eWMZ\nzkJtN68W8Wf28dXTHuTCukN+1aPLT/P6plfuqKMUkTnUdC+Lt3qdtsX/P9oM1PB2\nMSG5IHslLJBFMi3mr80PXet+/LKyzVPrFwi9q6SUENGjRgJrtuy6cPoLBuPVcht4\nqpz2FVxS0XTbjHPpIyhPkMAUin0tIbGUDvnetkCE6TEUZV7IBT20n+j7kAbe90iA\nCfpFiAD+s78qs2sNKDxNpRTA3tOu3rUOncVz4Ouc3LUpf29stY1CaWSnZ43q56gi\nKt29QgRmobfMvyypG75pEZrCaS3MnOid5uCfBNuuzrwozrr/kYnTklgnudrOKXte\nL4BbRT+Cs56xEPpF/1PzDjzhnkSeklHUqvFL54v4K9QpcdHwRxSNSqIX9+Aamavr\nlcZS8Hq1BwJL7iObZU9BDx2pFBn0Uq0OuedezLIv4xlk8FnaFdGScgP6y7LaUg8k\nhoVDJ9fCSttqv+p2TKp5wO+zaiXvdIGPhB6QBoSr1c90VvN9c38t9LkDai6SH1fG\n7VGVMgm6Kn3EKea06zNT\n=zXpv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:39:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72","node_id":"C_kwDOU_T1lNoAKDE1YTdiNTdmOGVkMzJjYjAyZWEwODQ0NDgwNjUxOWI0OWY0MjBiNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commit/e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0","sha":"e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0"}],"sha":"15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/15a7b57f8ed32cb02ea08444806519b49f420b72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56427313?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrewEhlo","id":56427313,"login":"AndrewEhlo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDI3MzEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/commits/e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T04:18:27Z","email":"56427313+AndrewEhlo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Andrew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T04:18:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(VCST-5970): guard workflows to upstream, add theme mirror build and sync (#2530)\n\n## Description\n\nThis repo is about to be synced into a private theme mirror, which will\nhold demo theme branches (`clone/<prospect>-<version>`). This PR makes\nthat safe: upstream workflows do nothing in the mirror, and the mirror''s\nown workflows do nothing here.\n\n**Behaviour in vc-frontend itself does not change.** Forks are affected:\nupstream workflows are now skipped on a fork''s own pushes and\ndispatches, because a fork is not this repository either. A fork that\nwants its own CI has to change the guard in its copy. PRs from forks\ninto vc-frontend are not affected; they run in this repository''s\ncontext, as before.\n\n**1. Repository guards on every existing job.**\n- Each job''s `if:` now starts with `github.repository_id ==\n''296335982''`, the id of VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend. The id is used\ninstead of the name because this repo has been renamed before (from\nvc-theme-b2b-vue). A name-based guard would silently skip every job\nafter the next rename, and with no required checks on `dev`, PRs would\nthen merge with no CI at all.\n- Existing conditions are kept after `&&`, in parentheses wherever they\ncontain `||`. Jobs that had no `if:` (release, core-facade-release,\ntheme-release-hotfix, deploy-cloud, pin-check) get the guard alone.\n- A skipped job takes no runner, so guarded workflows cost the mirror\nnothing.\n\n**2. Two mirror-only workflows.** Both have a `-mirror` suffix and are\nguarded by `vars.THEME_MIRROR == ''true''`. Only the mirror sets that\nrepository variable; this repo and forks do not, so neither workflow\nruns here.\n- `build-theme-mirror.yml` builds a `clone/*` branch on every push to\nit, or on manual dispatch. A newer push cancels an older in-flight build\nof the same branch.\n- The version is set with `jq`, not `yarn version`, so the single `yarn\ninstall --immutable` checks the committed lockfile.\n- Third-party install scripts are off. The blob SAS is passed only to\nthe publish step.\n- The artifact URL is published as a `theme-artifact` run artifact\n(`artifact-url.json`), so a consumer can pick the build of a branch''s\ncurrent head commit.\n- Prospect branches must be cut from a release that contains this PR, or\nnewer.\n- `sync-upstream-mirror.yml` pushes this repo''s `dev` and tags into the\nmirror, daily and on demand.\n- It never uses `--force`, `--mirror` or `--prune`, so `clone/*`\nbranches are never touched. A diverged `dev` or a moved tag fails the\nrun instead of being overwritten.\n  - Tags keep syncing while `dev` waits for recovery.\n- The file header lists the mirror setup (including Dependabot), the\nrecovery steps, and one known limitation of the push key on the Free\nplan.\n- Both workflows have to live here because scheduled and dispatched\nworkflows must exist on the mirror''s default branch, which is the synced\n`dev`.\n\n**3. `workflow-guards.yml`.** This PR check fails when a job''s `if:`:\n- does not start with one of the two guards;\n- has anything but `&&` right after the guard;\n- has a top-level `||` after the guard;\n- has a second `${{ }}` (a split expression is always true);\n- has unbalanced quotes;\n- or comes from a workflow file yq cannot read.\n\nThe convention is documented in `.github/workflows/README.md`.\n\n**What to check in review:**\n- the combined `if:` conditions in `theme-ci.yml`, `storybook-ci.yml`,\n`security.yml` and `codeql.yml` are logically unchanged for this repo;\n- CI on this PR runs as usual (Theme CI, CodeQL, Security, pin-check),\nplus the new guard check.\n\nThe mirror-only workflows are exercised only once the mirror exists.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5970\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2530-09c6-09c602fc.zip\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes when CI, releases, and deploys run across upstream, forks, and\na private mirror; incorrect guards could skip required checks or run\nsensitive jobs in the wrong repo, though vc-frontend itself should\nbehave as before.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Introduces **repository guards** so GitHub Actions run in the right\nplace: upstream jobs only when `github.repository_id == ''296335982''`\n(rename-proof `vc-frontend` id), and new mirror jobs only when\n`vars.THEME_MIRROR == ''true''`. Existing workflow conditions are\npreserved behind `&&` (with `||` wrapped in parentheses where needed).\n**Upstream behavior on this repo is unchanged**; the same guard skips CI\non forks unless they edit the guard locally.\n> \n> Adds two **mirror-only** workflows: **`build-theme-mirror.yml`**\nbuilds `clone/*` prospect branches, publishes a theme zip to blob\nstorage, and uploads `artifact-url.json` as a run artifact;\n**`sync-upstream-mirror.yml`** syncs upstream `dev` and tags into the\nmirror on a schedule (with divergence/moved-tag safety and optional\n`reset_dev` recovery).\n> \n> Adds **`workflow-guards.yml`** on PRs that touch workflows to enforce\nthe guard convention, and documents it in\n**`.github/workflows/README.md`**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n09c602fc07a78481a2102a0baf522000ce4aa399. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73c603e1c91f51beff19ddcfc5de20c1d7d5fa72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/trees/73c603e1c91f51beff19ddcfc5de20c1d7d5fa72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/commits/e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0","verification":{"payload":"tree 73c603e1c91f51beff19ddcfc5de20c1d7d5fa72\nparent e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d\nauthor Andrew <56427313+AndrewEhlo@users.noreply.github.com> 1790914707 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790914707 +0500\n\nci(VCST-5970): guard workflows to upstream, add theme mirror build and sync (#2530)\n\n## Description\n\nThis repo is about to be synced into a private theme mirror, which will\nhold demo theme branches (`clone/<prospect>-<version>`). This PR makes\nthat safe: upstream workflows do nothing in the mirror, and the mirror''s\nown workflows do nothing here.\n\n**Behaviour in vc-frontend itself does not change.** Forks are affected:\nupstream workflows are now skipped on a fork''s own pushes and\ndispatches, because a fork is not this repository either. A fork that\nwants its own CI has to change the guard in its copy. PRs from forks\ninto vc-frontend are not affected; they run in this repository''s\ncontext, as before.\n\n**1. Repository guards on every existing job.**\n- Each job''s `if:` now starts with `github.repository_id ==\n''296335982''`, the id of VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend. The id is used\ninstead of the name because this repo has been renamed before (from\nvc-theme-b2b-vue). A name-based guard would silently skip every job\nafter the next rename, and with no required checks on `dev`, PRs would\nthen merge with no CI at all.\n- Existing conditions are kept after `&&`, in 