0787d0b29c402f3ed0b32f2b776f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T11:30:16Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T11:30:16Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"message":"fix(VCST-6030): the rewards banner''s button says what it opens, and only when it opens\n\nThe button carries the design''s own label — \"Rewards catalog\", not the bare\n\"Catalog\" the key had been holding unused in all 13 module locales since the\nfeature shipped. Every language takes the wording its own description already\nuses for that catalog.\n\nAnd it is only a button when there is somewhere to go. The route needs a\ncurrency and a mode of Mixed Cart or Loyalty Store on top of the module being\non, while Missions needs only the module and its own flag, so a store with\nmissions and no catalog would have shown a button straight into NotFound. The\nbanner already draws its button on `v-if=\"linkTo\"`, so withholding the target\nwithholds the control.\n\nThe condition was a private copy inside the router reading the module settings\nby hand; it moves to useLoyaltySettings, beside the currency it already reads,\nand the four route guards keep asking the same question they asked before.","tree":{"sha":"96deababf55e518a0ef43b06115ab621b0834ba5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/trees/96deababf55e518a0ef43b06115ab621b0834ba5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend-next/git/commits/c6348a5d97d0787d0b29c402f3ed0b32f2b776f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}"