in":"maximsan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzY5OTEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximsan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximsan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximsan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximsan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximsan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maximsan/microfrontend-learn/commits/19a756da7720bcb826d902e26a79ec1c2dc4205f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:42:28Z","email":"maksim.shchytski@gmail.com","name":"maximsan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:42:28Z","email":"maksim.shchytski@gmail.com","name":"maximsan"},"message":"docs: close the gaps two reviews found in the trunk-based guide\n\nBoth reviewers noted the same holes. Branch prefixes covered only five\nof the eight commit types. Nothing said how to merge once --no-ff was\ngone, or who tags a release. The starter run read as if it had to\npass. Rejected findings had nowhere to be recorded.\n\nNow: <type>/<topic> for any type; merge with --no-ff, never squash;\nreleases ship from chore/release-X.Y.Z and only the maintainer tags;\nrejected findings go in the merge commit body. The README also says\nthe hosted copy is built from a release tag.","tree":{"sha":"751a4255894dece48e11b7ba110dbd4c281952c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maximsan/microfrontend-learn/git/trees/751a4255894dece48e11b7ba110dbd4c281952c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maximsan/microfrontend-learn/git/commits/19a756da7720bcb826d902e26a79ec1c2dc4205f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19369912?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximsan/events{/